{"type":"node-terminal","flowRunId":"01a04d7f-22e4-7693-bc57-3219f0ceecd4","ordinal":3,"dedupKey":"flow:01a04d7f-22e4-7693-bc57-3219f0ceecd4:k:spec-build:v1:gate:cp-build:checkpoint-cp-build","disposition":"created","taskUuid":"01a04d7f-37be-74f3-9128-7479551aab0b","verdict":"failed","witnessSeq":7526,"exitCode":1,"taskRef":"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/cp-build","stderrExcerpt":"......................................F\n======================================================================\nFAIL: test_worklist_shape_and_hygiene (test_repo_invariants.RepoInvariants.test_worklist_shape_and_hygiene)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/a6a018c7b64a/cp-build/tests/test_repo_invariants.py\", line 78, in test_worklist_shape_and_hygiene\n    self.assertNotIn(banned, raw.lower(),\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n                     f\"banned token '{banned}' in worklist bytes\")\n                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAssertionError: 'claude' unexpectedly found in '{\\n  \"schemaversion\": 1,\\n  \"campaign\": {\\n    \"name\": \"flashnext\",\\n    \"maxtasks\": 16,\\n    \"maxparallel\": 1,\\n    \"steward\": \"narrator\",\\n    \"agent\": {\\n      \"adapter\": \"claude-code\",\\n      \"approvalpolicy\": null,\\n      \"sandboxpolicy\": null,\\n      \"diagnosissandboxpolicy\": null,\\n      \"runtimemaxsec\": 14400\\n    },\\n    \"gates\": [\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"command\",\\n        \"id\": \"repo-tests\",\\n        \"preflightargv\": [\\n          \"sh\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"command -v python3 >/dev/null\"\\n        ],\\n        \"argv\": [\\n          \"python3\",\\n          \"-m\",\\n          \"unittest\",\\n          \"discover\",\\n          \"-s\",\\n          \"tests\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"command\",\\n        \"id\": \"spec-lint\",\\n        \"preflightargv\": [\\n          \"sh\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"test -d /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix\"\\n        ],\\n        \"argv\": [\\n          \"bash\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"nix develop /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix --command cargo run --manifest-path /home/tom/mecattaf/tally.nix/cargo.toml -q -p spec-lint -- specs/flashnext --worklist silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json --root . || [ $? -eq 1 ]\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"command\",\\n        \"id\": \"flake-eval\",\\n        \"preflightargv\": [\\n          \"sh\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"command -v nix >/dev/null\"\\n        ],\\n        \"argv\": [\\n          \"nix\",\\n          \"flake\",\\n          \"check\",\\n          \"--no-build\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"command\",\\n        \"id\": \"fork-verify\",\\n        \"preflightargv\": [\\n          \"sh\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"command -v git >/dev/null\"\\n        ],\\n        \"argv\": [\\n          \"bash\",\\n          \"scripts/verify-fork.sh\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"kind\": \"command\",\\n        \"id\": \"receipts-verify\",\\n        \"preflightargv\": [\\n          \"sh\",\\n          \"-euc\",\\n          \"command -v python3 >/dev/null\"\\n        ],\\n        \"argv\": [\\n          \"python3\",\\n          \"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"tasks\": [\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"container-recipe\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\",\\n      \"goal\": \"the primary engine lane of spec ruling p4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). write container/containerfile and container/build.sh implementing imports.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. containerfile: ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for gpu target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); copy container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\\\"build\\\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. credit the recipe shape to the mit toolbox recipe named in third_party_notices.md in the containerfile header. boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"a reproducible image build from the fork at the exactly pinned wheel set\",\\n        \"a build receipt the receipts gate can grade\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3\",\\n          \"imports.md\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"recipe-pins\",\\n          \"description\": \"the recipe pins the exact wheel set, the fork branch, and the image tag, and is syntax-clean.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"bash -n container/build.sh && grep -q \\'torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0\\' container/containerfile && grep -q \\'repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch\\' container/containerfile && grep -q \\'mecattaf/vllm\\' container/containerfile && grep -q \\'flashnext:dev\\' container/build.sh && grep -qi \\'mit\\' container/containerfile\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"container\",\\n        \"results/receipts\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"instruments\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay\",\\n      \"goal\": \"create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the fn_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a fn_profile window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env fn_offload_store_batch_frac and fn_offload_promote_frac), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env fn_expert_union with fn_eu_start, fn_eu_calls, fn_eu_out). every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"instruments importable inside the image with fn_ kill-switches, default off\",\\n        \"notice headers travel with every adapted module\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"instruments-compile-with-notices\",\\n          \"description\": \"all three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l \\'adapted from\\' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"container/rootfs\",\\n        \"tests\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"host-tooling\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"pair-service orchestration: env doctrine, cluster up/down, first-light runner\",\\n      \"goal\": \"write the host/ tooling and scripts/run-tp2.sh per spec claims 4.2, 4.3, 4.4, 4.5 and 6.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4, #r6), composing the disciplines in specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 5 and specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md section 5. host/fn-env.sh: pythonhashseed=0; pytorch_hip_alloc_conf=expandable_segments:true,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85; hsa_enable_interrupt=1; inductor and triton cache dirs under the state directory, never tmpfs; nccl_socket_ifname set only to the thunderbolt rails that carry a routable /30 ip (rail 0 thunderbolt0/10.99.0.x is guaranteed; rail 1 thunderbolt1 is trained-but-ip-unconfigured today per dotfiles modules/lowlat-cluster.nix and must not be listed until it has a peer ip — a peerless link-local rail in the list hangs rccl bootstrap; the env file computes this from `ip -br addr` at write time and logs which rails it chose, rather than hardcoding both); nccl_ib_disable=1 unconditionally (an ibverbs device now exists on the rails from the pre-arm bake; without this pin rccl autodetects verbs and silently rides unproven rdma — sockets are the transport of record until the attended morning a/b, evidence host/rdma/ab-protocol.md); vllm_ray_extra_env_var_prefixes_to_copy=fn_; vllm_ple_mmap=1; a loud comment forbidding exports of engine defaults read through is-set probes. host/fn-cluster-up.sh: podman on both nodes (worker over ssh on the wire), distributed head on the coordinator and worker join, worker python pool capped small, a hard two-gpu gate before serve, then the serve process at tensor-parallel size 2 with eager execution, model directory /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8, served name flashnext; reap stranded serve processes before start and gate on zero residue. host/fn-cluster-down.sh: idempotent teardown both nodes. host/fn-preflight.sh: byte-diff of both ranks\\' fn_ env, latency-hold device read on both ends, per-rail link-speed record, round-trip probe on both rails. host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service: oneshot, remainafterexit, execstoppost teardown, no install section. scripts/run-tp2.sh: preflight, up, two greedy 300-token completions byte-compared, residency read after 50 warmed decode tokens (gtt per rank from sysfs plus process rss plus table page-cache residency), fidelity capture (fixed-prompt losses and frontier logits under results/), then a 262144-context probe, writing receipts tp2.json, residency.json, fidelity.json, context.json per the receipts-verify.py schema. extend tests/test_repo_invariants.py-adjacent coverage with tests/test_host_tooling.py asserting the env file carries the doctrine lines and unit files carry execstoppost and no wantedby install. boundaries: touch only host/, scripts/run-tp2.sh, and tests/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"one command stands the pair service; one command tears it down; failure cannot strand ranks\",\\n        \"first light produces the four receipts the ladder grades\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"scripts/stage-weights.sh\",\\n          \"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"host-doctrine\",\\n          \"description\": \"env doctrine present, units teardown-safe, all scripts syntax-clean, host tests pass.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"for f in host/*.sh scripts/run-tp2.sh; do bash -n \\\\\"$f\\\\\"; done && grep -q \\'pythonhashseed=0\\' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q \\'nccl_socket_ifname\\' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q \\'thunderbolt0\\' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q \\'nccl_ib_disable=1\\' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q \\'vllm_ray_extra_env_var_prefixes_to_copy=fn_\\' host/fn-env.sh && grep -q \\'execstoppost\\' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && ! grep -q \\'wantedby\\' host/systemd/flashnext-pair.service && python3 -m unittest tests.test_host_tooling -v\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"host\",\\n        \"scripts/run-tp2.sh\",\\n        \"tests\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"bench-harness\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix\",\\n      \"goal\": \"write bench/fn-stream-client.py and bench/run-matrix.sh per spec claims 6.2 and 6.3 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6). the client measures per-request time-to-first-token client-side and scrapes the server metrics endpoint to separate scheduler queue wait from prompt processing — the reference harness\\'s client published a prefill column that duplicated its first-token column (specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md section 4.4); ours must not. emit csv with explicit column semantics in a header comment, plus a sha256 fingerprint of every completion\\'s token ids. run-matrix.sh: arms interleaved a-b-b-a, three loads per arm, medians reported, depth series 0, 10240, 102400 tokens, speculative decoding on and off arms, results committed under results/ and a bench.json receipt {loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}. add tests/test_bench_client.py: feed the client parser a fixture with known queue and processing times and assert the two columns separate them. boundaries: touch only bench/ and tests/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"a client whose prefill number is a measurement, not a proxy\",\\n        \"a matrix whose every number carries its protocol\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"bench-honest-client\",\\n          \"description\": \"client compiles, separation test passes, matrix script is syntax-clean.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"python3 -m py_compile bench/fn-stream-client.py && bash -n bench/run-matrix.sh && python3 -m unittest tests.test_bench_client -v\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"bench\",\\n        \"tests\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"proxy-tooling\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"proxy checkpoint builder and single-node first-light runner\",\\n      \"goal\": \"re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-fp8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork\\'s tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with vllm_ple_mmap=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the api, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later tp=2 serve reproduce them. the serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (json quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set vllm_rocm_apu_unified_memory, since the host logs integrated_gpu=false and that steer was superseded. pytorch_hip_alloc_conf=expandable_segments:true is optional. (3) any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live gpu first light. the scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"the admitted kernel path and the ported table path execute on this gpu before any real weight byte is loaded\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r4\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/ple-54129.md\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/moe-dispatch.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"scripts/run-smoke.sh\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"proxy-scripts-clean\",\\n          \"description\": \"both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q \\'results/receipts/proxy.json\\' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\\n          ]\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"proxy-serve-flags\",\\n          \"description\": \"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap ple path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling oom.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"grep -q \\'vllm_ple_mmap=1\\' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q \\'limit-mm-per-prompt\\' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qe \\'enforce.eager|enforce_eager\\' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q \\'skip-mm-profiling\\' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\\n          ]\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"proxy-checkpoint-layout\",\\n          \"description\": \"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-fp8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork\\'s test scaffolding.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"grep -q \\'/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy\\' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q \\'weight_block_size\\' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q \\'128\\' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q \\'tests/models\\' scripts/make-proxy.sh\"\\n          ]\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"proxy-lane-clean\",\\n          \"description\": \"the lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task\\'s commit.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"[ -z \\\\\"$(git status --porcelain)\\\\\" ]\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [\\n        \"container-recipe\"\\n      ],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\\n        \"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\\n        \"tests\",\\n        \"results/receipts/proxy.json\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"morning-ledger\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"render the morning ledger and the announcement draft\",\\n      \"goal\": \"write docs/morning.md per spec claim 6.4 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6): a receipt review table (one row per receipt under results/receipts with status and the bound it was graded against), the open-items list (every unknown from the spec with its drain state), the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling p13), the optimization menu (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this gpu, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame a-b, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from imports.md), and a blocker template implementing ruling p16. also write docs/announce.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 gb unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. boundaries: touch only docs/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"the operator\\'s first ten minutes are a checklist, not archaeology\",\\n        \"the community post is ready to publish with the benchmark numbers\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7\",\\n          \"imports.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"readme.md\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"ledger-sections\",\\n          \"description\": \"the ledger carries its five sections and the announcement draft exists.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"grep -q \\'receipt review\\' docs/morning.md && grep -q \\'open items\\' docs/morning.md && grep -q \\'promotion checklist\\' docs/morning.md && grep -q \\'optimization menu\\' docs/morning.md && grep -qi \\'blocker\\' docs/morning.md && test -s docs/announce.md\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [\\n        \"host-tooling\",\\n        \"bench-harness\"\\n      ],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"docs\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"catalog-handoff\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"prepare the fleet catalog patch for the morning operator\",\\n      \"goal\": \"write handoff/catalog-row.patch per spec claim 5.2 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5): a git format patch against the fleet configuration repository adding the workload checkpoint as a snapshot-layout artifact row assigned to both hosts, following the existing snapshot-layout precedent row in that repository\\'s model library file, with pinned upstream revision and per-file byte counts read from the staged copy under /var/lib/local-models/flashnext-fp8 (or from the library mount when staging has not finished). add handoff/readme.md explaining exactly what the operator applies and verifies in the morning. the patch is prepared, never applied, by this campaign. boundaries: touch only handoff/.\",\\n      \"deliveredbehaviors\": [\\n        \"the morning catalog declaration is one git apply plus one review, not authoring work\"\\n      ],\\n      \"readfirst\": {\\n        \"specsections\": [\\n          \"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r5\",\\n          \"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"\\n        ],\\n        \"stylereferences\": [\\n          \"third_party_notices.md\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"acceptancecriteria\": [\\n        {\\n          \"id\": \"catalog-patch-wellformed\",\\n          \"description\": \"the patch parses as a git patch and the handoff note exists.\",\\n          \"argv\": [\\n            \"bash\",\\n            \"-euc\",\\n            \"git apply --stat handoff/catalog-row.patch >/dev/null && test -s handoff/readme.md\"\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"dependencies\": [],\\n      \"conflictdomains\": [\\n        \"handoff\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"rdma-package\",\\n      \"kind\": \"implementation\",\\n      \"title\": \"integrate the operator-attended rdma package under host/rdma\",\\n      \"goal\": \"the bootstrap session scoped an operator-attended rdma bring-up package (spec ruling p7, claim 6.4 — specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6): host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh (pinned out-of-tree module fetch, kernel-version and secure-boot guards, staged install only), host/rdma/attended-bringup.md (the coordinated-reboot checklist with the port-controller recovery path), host/rdma/ab-protocol.md (the socket-ve